The Pudding Guy · 3D YouTube Short (1080×1920)

Picture: modelled, lit and animated in code with three.js (MIT). Post (depth of field, ambient occlusion, bloom, grade):
core/three/post.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT). Characters (sculpted heads with
painted faces), sets (a 1999 suburb, a supermarket, a food-bank hall, an airliner) and props are built from primitives for
this film. The people are stylised stand-ins with no real likeness; the pudding brand ("Choco Cup"), the store ("Super
Save") and the airline livery are invented.

Voice-over: generated with ElevenLabs v4 (voice preset "Harrison") through the creator's Higgsfield account; pauses tightened
and the read sped up 15 % (pitch unchanged) in timing.py. Check Higgsfield's / ElevenLabs' terms for your use.

Font: Fredoka — Milena Brandão / Google Fonts, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL-Fredoka.txt).

Music and sound effects: synthesized in code (music.py; synth_lib.py from the Lemo-Opuscar library, MIT). No samples.
